    "difficultyReason": "The first line of the proof is given, and the task tells the student to split the fraction. What remains is index-law simplification: 3^{-2x}/3^{-x} = 3^{-x} and 1/3^{-x} = 3^x. The student then repeats the split for f(x) and compares it with f(-x). This is a routine linked procedure with two small index-law decisions and no open choice of method. It is more demanding than the even/odd checks in p9-q2-block, because those use direct substitution with no manipulation of negative exponents. It is easier than the unscaffolded version of this proof (p10-q7).",
